I just finished a fun game of Sporkhack and was racing to finish
before the savebreak today.  I died to a team attack of an angel, a
master mind flayer and Famine.  Famine stunned me and the mind flayer
sucked my brains out.  I have to say, the denizens of the Astral Plane
sure have bigger teeth in Sporkhack!  Burned through at least half a
dozen potions of full healing just through running the gauntlet of
priests and angels.

Died with multiple death and teleport zaps remaining, an unused wand
of wishing, and oh yeah, an amulet of life saving :/.  I should have
taken on the mind flayer and Famine one-on-one instead of trying to
skip around them.  Have mind flayers always been immune to being
teleported away from a broken wand of teleport?

Derek, you've made some nice changes!  The game takes me almost twice
as long now (died at the wrong altar at turn 44k) since most of
Gehennom is both non-teleport and more of a challenge than Nethack.  I
only used 1 wish since it turns out that the castle chest with the
wand of wishing was my teleport test subject.  The new castle turrets
do allow for the hero to teleport the chests potentially out of the
castle.  I didn't find the chest until the ascension run and I never
bothered to use it.  I also went genocide-less so that I could
experience the Lich changes.  They were pesky but the lack of self-
teleport in Gehennom is pretty well-balanced with Master Liches no
longer being covetous.

I like create familiar and was planning on testing the implications of
it being level 3 while on Astral.  I suppose I should have done so
_before_ I died.  I was actually thinking that it could be well used
and I wish I had given it a try.  My thinking was that since I had 180-
something Pw and an amulet of Power I could have started creating
peaceful monsters and with a magic whistle just displaced my way
through Astral.  I also kept a bunch of scrolls and wands of create
monster and was planning on zapping those after I had surrounded
myself with peacefuls.  I suppose that hostile missile and range
attacks would have thinned them out, though.  If I get there again
I'll give it a try.

